/*
:name: loop_lec_index_2
:lec_set: formal.lec.semdiff=none
:lec_grep: loop certificate: 1 matched compact recurrence
:lec_grep: "loop_certificates":".*P0=descriptor-exact.*P4/P5=ordinal-recurrence
*/
// HEADER-ONLY variant: no Pyrope code, so the source is loop_lec_index.prp
// itself and the two sides share its `:set:` flags. That makes this the SELF
// check — one compact loop against itself.
//
// It is not a tautology: with semdiff's structural shortcut turned OFF, the
// matched form has to reuse the ONE body theorem and report every M6 premise
// (`:lec_grep:`) instead of materializing the four ordinals. Losing the
// certificate would still say PROVEN, just by re-proving the body per ordinal —
// which is precisely the cost M6 exists to avoid.
